  "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, we first approximate the value of the radical using a calculator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{15\\times 11}=\\sqrt{165}≈‭‭12.845\\,233\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nNow, we approximate the value of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2.5\\sqrt{15\\times 11} & ≈ \\\\ 2.5\\times ‭‭12.845\\,233 & ≈ \\\\ 32.113\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
